# Suricata alert suppression and thresholds (wired in via --set=threshold-file in docker-compose.yml)
# Blocks alerts "only under this condition" instead of disabling whole rules. Record cause and evidence in docs/tuning-log.md for every entry.
#
# Format: suppress gen_id <gid>, sig_id <sid>, track <by_src|by_dst|by_either>, ip <address|CIDR>

# TUNE-001 (2026-09-14) the sensor's own requests to the GCE metadata server
#   - the guest agent requests /computeMetadata/v1/instance/credentials/mds-client-certificate with Go-http-client every minute
#   - host scripts request /computeMetadata/v1/instance/?recursive=true with curl
#   169.254.169.254 is a link-local address that never leaves the VM, so user-agent rules are suppressed for this destination only.
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 2024897, track by_dst, ip 169.254.169.254
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 2060251, track by_dst, ip 169.254.169.254
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 2034567, track by_dst, ip 169.254.169.254

# TUNE-018 (2026-09-15) the sensor's own Python tooling fetching metadata-server tokens over plain HTTP
#   - nsm-honeypot-pull (every minute), nsm-responder's reconciler (every 30 s in enforce mode) and gcloud use
#     urllib against /computeMetadata/v1/…, which matches ET INFO Python-urllib Suspicious User Agent (~55–250 alerts/h)
#   Same link-local destination as TUNE-001, so only that destination is suppressed.
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 2013031, track by_dst, ip 169.254.169.254
